  "methods": {
    "controller": "Native ROA student with estimated velocity. Seed 42; fixed-plane cases keep trained dynamics randomization and disable timed pushes. Each fixed trial has one environment and 1,000 control steps at 0.02 s.",
    "feet": "Steps 200..749, four 5 ms physics samples per tick. Support is upward force >=5 N. Median swing apex and integrated contact-point slip use complete swings and stances only. Qualified touchdown requires a complete swing of >=40 ms with >=5 mm apex.",
    "limits": "Per-joint maximum absolute telemetry value divided by the simulator joint limit over all 1,000 control samples. These are 20 ms samples. Torque and joint speed are not 5 ms foot telemetry.",
    "steady": "Control steps 200..749 (4 <= t < 15 s) within the first episode. Body forward and yaw are signed body-frame means. World heading change uses unwrapped wxyz quaternion yaw over steps 100..749 and truncates at first reset. Long-left matches the standard command up to step 749.",
    "stop": "From 2 s after command release until step 999 or first reset. No post-reset samples are joined. Stand uses the same late analysis window as the main cases.",
    "training_distribution": "32 environments, 2000 control steps each. Use original terrain, command resampling, pushes, noise and 20 s time limit. Termination counts are termination rate multiplied by 64,000 environment steps. XY and yaw errors use the evaluator metric accumulators."
  },
